# Lines scripts/check-merged-wording.sh accepts even though they say "merged"
# outside the accepted tokens (`merged`, outcome=merged, pr_state=merged,
# MERGED, unmerged, not-merged).
#
# Format, tab-separated, three fields:
#
#   <file>  <match>  <reason>
#
#   file    repository-relative path; must be one of the files the check scans
#   match   a fixed string (not a regex) that matches exactly one line of file
#   reason  why that line describes GitHub PR state rather than a run outcome;
#           required, an empty reason is an error
#
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored. The check fails on a record whose
# match finds zero lines or more than one, on a stale record (its line no
# longer says "merged" outside the accepted tokens), on an empty reason, and on
# a file outside the scanned list, so a record here stays tied to one line
# that still needs it.
#
# Prefer rewording over a record. A record belongs only where the natural
# sentence is about what GitHub reports for a PR and the accepted tokens would
# read worse. The scanned files currently need none.
